-   *
-   * You can declare a test as to be fixed, and Playwright will not run it.
-   *
-   * ```js
-   * import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
-   *
-   * test.fixme('to be fixed', async ({ page }) => {
-   *   // ...
-   * });
-   * ```
